1. Abstract

This system provides illustrations of biological reactions, signal 
transductions, gene expressions and their relationships using Quixote.

2. Configuration

Knowledge Base Module ..........Signal Transduction Pathway
Interface Module ...............Pathway Viewing and Query Processing
External DB Interface Module ...PIR access 

3. Features

(1) KB Module

The aspect of the object oriented database language of Quixote enables 
to represent pieces of biological processes systematically and easily.
And the aspect of the deductive database language provides total 
illustration from the pieces of biological processes which may be altered 
or detailed.

(2) IF Module

GUI shows biological processes in the requested minuteness.

(3) DB Module

References to the existing public databases such as PIR or ProSite 
are available.

4. Environment

Machine     : UNIX Workstation(tested in IRIS, Sparc10)
Environment : UNIX, X Window(Motif)
Language    : C, C++, yacc/lex
Source Code : 190KB

